<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Export-compliance declaration for the App Store.

    On macOS the app performs ALL cryptography via Apple's operating system and
    implements/bundles no cryptographic algorithm of its own: RSA key generation
    uses Security.framework (SecKeyCreateRandomKey), and the private-key password
    encryption (PBKDF2 + AES-256-CBC) uses CommonCrypto. See
    src-tauri/src/crypto_apple.rs — the der/pkcs8/pkcs1/spki/pkcs5 crates there
    only serialize ASN.1/PEM, they do not encrypt.

    Because the encryption is "limited to encryption within Apple's operating
    system", the app qualifies for that exemption, so this is set to false — no
    App Encryption Documentation / self-classification upload is required.

    NOTE: the off-Apple (Windows/Linux) builds DO bundle RustCrypto algorithms;
    this declaration only governs the macOS App Store build. Final classification
    is the submitter's responsibility.
    Ref: https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/complying-with-encryption-export-regulations
  -->
  <key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
